{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\np='assurance_node_proposal_test.go'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('\\\"event\\\": \\\"propose_after_leadership_change\\\", \\\"step\\\": \\\"propose-after-leadership-change\\\"','\\\"event\\\": \\\"propose_after_campaign_attempt\\\", \\\"step\\\": \\\"propose-after-campaign-attempt\\\"')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Record the repair-path attempt for the Node-wrapper question. The retained receipt already establishes the witness; this update adds what the native attempt at the leadership-change control showed (node 2 campaigned, leader 1 rejected its vote, so the leadership never changed and the channel stayed closed) and keeps that as an unmeasured limitation rather than a result. The draft harness now names that observation for what it is (a campaign attempt), and no execution is requested for it.\\\",\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"7f6aa45d046c4714992282dd5e6d8389-experiment\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"node-propc-guard\\\",\\\"node-propc-restore\\\",\\\"node-propose-block\\\",\\\"node-propose-doc\\\"],\n  \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d\\\":[1,2,3,4]},\n  \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\n  \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The account's substance is unchanged and rests on receipt 8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d: node.run closes the proposal channel when an applied change removes the local node and restores it only in the branch that reacts to a change of r.lead with a leader known (node.go:400-432 and node.go:343-380), Node.Propose sends into that channel and a nil channel turns the call into a wait for the caller's context (node.go:514-551), and the receipt shows the control holding before the removal (parsed index 1: no error, 0ms, the leader's log index advances to 2) and the witness violated afterwards (parsed index 4: with the leader's configuration back to voters=(1 2), node 2 caught up and still knowing leader 1 in term 1, Propose returns only when its 300ms deadline fires and the leader's log index stays at 4). What this update adds is the state of the restore path named in the question's discriminator. The draft harness now campaigns the re-added node and records the exchange: node 2 emitted one MsgVote at term 2, leader 1 answered with one rejecting MsgVoteResp, node 2 therefore lost the election and ended as a follower at term 2 with no known leader, and the following Propose call was still blocked (300ms, context deadline exceeded, the group's log unchanged at index 4). That run is a native draft observation, not a retained receipt, and it does not measure the restore path: the leadership did not change, so the branch that would re-open the channel was never exercised. The reason the campaign lost lies in the harness (a direct leader made through becomeCandidate/becomeLeader keeps Vote and lead pointing at itself, and the vote was rejected) rather than in the question, so the restore path stays unmeasured; the draft event was renamed to say 'campaign attempt' so that a future basis does not present it as a leadership-change observation.\\\",\n  \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n   \\\"The control comparison holds (parsed index 1) and both witness comparisons are violated (index 4) with a complete witness, so the measured claim does not depend on the restore-path attempt.\\\",\n   \\\"The Node.Propose documentation warns that proposals can be lost without notice (node.go:138-140), so a caller with a deadline and retries is not blocked; the defect is that the channel stays closed while the node is a member again and a leader is known.\\\",\n   \\\"The restore-path attempt did not change the leadership (the vote was rejected in the harness), so it neither confirms nor contradicts the source's statement that a leadership change re-opens the channel.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\n   \\\"The harness drives a wrapped node against a bare raft instance, so the wrapper's asynchronous ready/advance contract is exercised on one side only, and both nodes run in one process.\\\",\n   \\\"The proposed call uses a 300ms deadline; the receipt measures that the call did not complete within it and that the group's log did not change, not how long the channel stays closed in absolute terms.\\\",\n   \\\"The leadership-change restore path remains unmeasured: the draft's campaign attempt lost its election, and the reason lies in how the harness installs the leader rather than in the question, so a future basis must make the wrapped node win an election (or otherwise change r.lead while a leader is known) before the restore branch can be observed.\\\",\n   \\\"Whether an application is expected to keep proposing through a node that has been removed and re-added is itself part of the question; the library's own comment calls the current mechanism unsound rather than documenting an intended semantics.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"knowledge\\\":[\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-0\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"The proposal channel is closed by the removal guard and restored only by a leadership change with a leader known.\\\"},\n   {\\\"entry_id\\\":\\\"05a1b54cf0ce4ce0bcd9e888623b8fae-knowledge-1\\\",\\\"revision\\\":1,\\\"assertion\\\":\\\"With a nil proposal channel Propose blocks until the caller's context or the node's done channel fires.\\\"}\n  ]}]}\nopen('update17.json','w').write(json.dumps(u,indent=2)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_13-42-19-etcd_raft-real-run --submission update17.json 2>&1 | tail -4\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
