{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update17.json\",\"summary\":\"Recorded the state of the Node-wrapper restore path without overstating it. The measured account is unchanged and still rests on receipt 8b3e88d4b4a641fa8ddc723ecc0ba56d: the control holds (parsed index 1 - before the removal the same call returns no error in 0ms and the leader's log index advances to 2) and the witness is violated (parsed index 4 - with the leader's configuration back to voters=(1 2), node 2 caught up and still knowing leader 1 in term 1, Propose returns only when its 300ms deadline fires and the leader's log index stays at 4). What this update adds is what the native attempt at the leadership-change control showed: the draft harness now campaigns the re-added node and records the exchange - node 2 emitted one MsgVote at term 2, leader 1 answered with one rejecting MsgVoteResp, node 2 lost the election and ended as a follower at term 2 with no known leader, and the following Propose call was still blocked with the group's log unchanged. That run is a native draft observation, not a receipt, and it does not measure the restore path because the leadership never changed; the reason the campaign lost lies in how the harness installs the leader (a bare becomeCandidate/becomeLeader keeps Vote and lead pointing at itself) rather than in the question, so the restore path stays unmeasured and is recorded as such, with the draft event renamed to 'campaign attempt' so a future basis cannot present it as a leadership-change observation. Counterevidence keeps the holding control, the violated witness and the documented proposal-loss warning; limitations keep the one-sided harness, the 300ms deadline, the unmeasured restore path with what a future basis must do to observe it, and the open question of the wrapper's intended semantics for a re-added node.\"}"}}
